From: use-frama-c cast/region investigation
Subject: [PATCH] wp/MemBytes: degrade gracefully on unknown-size arrays in protected_sizeof_object

Frama-C: 32.1 (Germanium)
File:    src/plugins/wp/MemBytes.ml
Target:  function protected_sizeof_object (the -wp-model bytes size machinery)

Problem
-------
Under -wp-model bytes, any function that needs the size of an unknown-size array
(extern `T a[]`, flexible array member, or a linker-section array such as Zephyr's
STRUCT_SECTION_FOREACH) aborts WP with a fatal internal error:

    Failure: Sizeof unknown-size array
    Plug-in wp aborted: internal error.

protected_sizeof_object guards only the opaque-struct case (C_comp {cfields=None});
its `obj` fallthrough calls Ctypes.sizeof_object, which raises Failure on a C_array
with no flat size. The Failure is not caught by BASE.sizeof's Warning.handle wrapper
(which catches Warning.error, not arbitrary Failure) and escapes as a kernel fatal.

The default Typed model handles the same input gracefully: MemTyped.length_of_object
returns max_int under -wp-extern-arrays, else raises a recoverable Warning.error that
hides the sub-term -- never a hard Failure.

Fix
---
Mirror MemTyped: guard the unknown-size C_array case (arr_flat = None) and degrade the
same way (max_int / recoverable Warning.error). Compilation-only; adds no Why3/Coq axiom
(does not touch the WP TCB).

Verified
--------
- Minimal repro `extern int tbl[]; int *g(void){ return &tbl[0]; }` and the section-loop
  idiom no longer abort under -wp-model bytes (graceful "Undefined array-size" warning).
- Real unit zephyr/kernel/mem_slab.c: FATAL -> 44/80 (vs Typed 43/80).
- Corpus-wide (35 Zephyr kernel units): no unit aborts; bytes >= Typed everywhere.

See ../bugs-to-report/wp-cast-region-soundness/REPORT-membytes-sizeof.md for full detail.
---
--- a/src/plugins/wp/MemBytes.ml	2026-06-23 11:38:23.651061371 +0200
+++ b/src/plugins/wp/MemBytes.ml	2026-06-23 11:38:23.651851402 +0200
@@ -201,6 +201,16 @@
 let protected_sizeof_object = function
   | C_comp ({ cfields = None } as c) ->
     e_fun (OPAQUE_COMP_LENGTH.get c) []
+  | C_array { arr_flat = None } as obj ->
+    (* Unknown-size array (extern/flexible/linker-section): Ctypes.sizeof_object
+       raises Failure here, which escapes as a plugin fatal. Degrade like MemTyped:
+       max_int under -wp-extern-arrays, else a recoverable Warning.error that hides
+       the term (caught by BASE.sizeof's Warning.handle / the per-goal Warning.catch). *)
+    if Wp_parameters.ExternArrays.get () then
+      e_int max_int
+    else
+      Warning.error ~source:"Bytes Model"
+        "Undefined array-size (%a)" Ctypes.pretty obj
   | obj -> e_int @@ Ctypes.sizeof_object obj
 
 (* ********************************************************************** *)
